*  badsyntax.sno -- a statement the compiler cannot read.
*  ERRORS: an opening parenthesis with nothing to close it. The
*  compiler reports it as an erroneous or missing break character,
*  which is the syntax tables of Appendix A saying they ran off the
*  end of what they were reading rather than off the end of the card.
*  Part of github.com/mdhender/sil. BSD 2-Clause; see LICENSE.
*
*  Every program in this set is compiled under a -UNLIST control card,
*  because the listing shares the printer with the program's output.
*  An invalid one turns it back on for itself, below, because the
*  listing is where the compiler names the card it could not read --
*  and after the header, so that the golden holds statements and not
*  this paragraph.
-LIST
        OUTPUT = (1 + 2
END
